(4114927, 586960, 50034, '<td valign="top"><b>Interesting Perspective on your Free Advertisement!  :)</b></td>', 'Interesting Perspective on your Free Advertisement!  :)', '2007-09-25 16:34:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4114929, 588274, 77192, '<td valign="top">great idea.<br/> <br/>Is it me or do the notes look like they''re made of plastic? (not judging your image on that at all, just curious lol)</td>', 'great idea. Is it me or do the notes look like they''re made of plastic? (not judging your image on that at all, just curious lol)', '2007-09-25 16:34:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4114931, 588374, 77192, '<td valign="top">I won''t vote on this shot but I will leave a comment, for reasons I won''t go into, but you might have worked out for yourself, and you''ll know for certain after voting is done. Sorry to be so enigmatic lol.<br/> <br/>I do love the angle, it''s very well composed and an interesting shot. And I can''t overemphasise how much I like the idea.<br/> <br/>There are a couple of things I''d have perhaps done differently though - the lighting, which I presume is from above and behind the "hotels", looks a little harsh, which has left the shadow underneath the car. Perhaps if you''d had another light source from the opposite side it would have evened it out a bit. Alternatively, you might have tried fill flash or (it might seem a bit odd but go with me on this one lol) dialled in a bit of overexposure. The other effect of the lighting is the purplish hue on the edge of the car.<br/> <br/>The other thing I''ve noticed is the texture of the car itself, I don''t know if it''s the processing you did but it seems a little oversharpened.<br/> <br/>But I''m nitpicking a bit, I do like the shot a lot. Sorry for the cryptic nature of this comment lol.</td>', 'I won''t vote on this shot but I will leave a comment, for reasons I won''t go into, but you might have worked out for yourself, and you''ll know for certain after voting is done. Sorry to be so enigmatic lol. I do love the angle, it''s very well composed and an interesting shot. And I can''t overemphasise how much I like the idea. There are a couple of things I''d have perhaps done differently though - the lighting, which I presume is from above and behind the "hotels", looks a little harsh, which has left the shadow underneath the car. Perhaps if you''d had another light source from the opposite side it would have evened it out a bit. Alternatively, you might have tried fill flash or (it might seem a bit odd but go with me on this one lol) dialled in a bit of overexposure. The other effect of the lighting is the purplish hue on the edge of the car. The other thing I''ve noticed is the texture of the car itself, I don''t know if it''s the processing you did but it seems a little oversharpened. But I''m nitpicking a bit, I do like the shot a lot. Sorry for the cryptic nature of this comment lol.', '2007-09-25 16:35:02.000000', NULL, 1),
